00:00:42,919 --> 00:00:45,750
can manage with help of that form in the

17
00:00:45,750 --> 00:00:46,091
end.

18
00:00:47,679 --> 00:00:50,289
Now you find the project attached and after

19
00:00:50,354 --> 00:00:53,194
downloading, you should run npm install to

20
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:55,970
install all dependencies and then npm start

21
00:00:55,970 --> 00:00:56,688
to start this development server.

22
00:00:58,652 --> 00:00:59,947
And once you did that,

23
00:01:00,579 --> 00:01:03,316
if you visit localhost:3000,

24
00:01:03,899 --> 00:01:05,664
you should see a page like this.

25
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:10,942
And now your job for this exercise is

26
00:01:11,618 --> 00:01:15,516
to use HTMX, which is already included in

27
00:01:15,549 --> 00:01:17,906
the starting project and loaded into this

28
00:01:17,906 --> 00:01:18,197
page,

29
00:01:18,876 --> 00:01:21,481
so you don't need to do that, but your job

30
00:01:21,481 --> 00:01:23,745
is to use HTMX to

31
00:01:24,487 --> 00:01:27,591
register the submission of this form and to

32
00:01:27,656 --> 00:01:28,723
then add a new

33
00:01:29,257 --> 00:01:29,386
goal,

34
00:01:30,308 --> 00:01:32,977
just the text that was entered by the user

35
00:01:33,305 --> 00:01:35,072
to this courseGoals array.

36
00:01:36,912 --> 00:01:39,456
And of course, since this array is then used

37
00:01:39,488 --> 00:01:41,066
down there to output the goals,

38
00:01:41,645 --> 00:01:43,980
you should make sure that the goals then do

39
00:01:44,093 --> 00:01:47,103
show up on the screen whenever the user did

40
00:01:47,232 --> 00:01:48,776
submit a new goal here.

41
00:01:49,693 --> 00:01:52,588
Now to complete this task, you will also

42
00:01:52,588 --> 00:01:55,190
need to register a new POST route here,

43
00:01:55,318 --> 00:01:58,077
which you can do with app.post, and you can

44
00:01:58,077 --> 00:02:00,354
simply follow the same approach we used

45
00:02:00,466 --> 00:02:03,625
before in this section here to then extract

46
00:02:03,738 --> 00:02:06,464
the submitted data, and then you just add

47
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:09,254
the submitted text to this courseGoals

48
00:02:09,511 --> 00:02:09,687
array.

49
00:02:10,409 --> 00:02:12,462
That should be all you need to do here.

50
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:15,364
And of course, as mentioned, you must make

51
00:02:15,364 --> 00:02:18,299
sure that any goals added by the user are

52
00:02:18,428 --> 00:02:19,951
then reflected on the screen.

53
00:02:21,475 --> 00:02:24,810
You might also notice that all these goals

54
00:02:24,987 --> 00:02:27,857
also have a remove button, but you don't

55
00:02:27,889 --> 00:02:29,926
need to do anything with that.

56
00:02:31,321 --> 00:02:33,855
Therefore, that's your task now, your

57
00:02:33,967 --> 00:02:36,934
exercise. Here's a short pause for you to

58
00:02:37,030 --> 00:02:39,083
pause the video and try this on your own.

59
00:02:39,677 --> 00:02:41,922
Thereafter, we'll solve this together.

60
00:02:46,253 --> 00:02:49,291
Let's now solve this task together and I'll

61
00:02:49,356 --> 00:02:51,808
start with handling the form submission.

62
00:02:52,776 --> 00:02:54,865
As you learned before, we can add the

63
00:02:54,946 --> 00:02:59,686
hx-post attribute to the form so that a POST

64
00:02:59,686 --> 00:03:02,004
request will be sent whenever the form is

65
00:03:02,055 --> 00:03:02,596
submitted.

66
00:03:04,252 --> 00:03:07,126
Now, the path to which this request should

67
00:03:07,158 --> 00:03:09,450
be sent is up to you because you

68
00:03:10,047 --> 00:03:13,050
own this backend code and here I'll send it

69
00:03:13,050 --> 00:03:13,478
to a

70
00:03:14,217 --> 00:03:16,874
/goals route. But again, that is up to you.

71
00:03:18,766 --> 00:03:20,570
Of course, we now must add such a

72
00:03:22,004 --> 00:03:24,453
/goals POST route here to this

73
00:03:25,146 --> 00:03:26,322
Express application,

74
00:03:26,918 --> 00:03:29,450
which we can do like this, just as we did it

75
00:03:29,450 --> 00:03:31,008
before in this section.

76
00:03:32,329 --> 00:03:34,903
And in here, I then get my goal text.

77
00:03:36,090 --> 00:03:38,503
Maybe let's name it goalText therefore

78
00:03:39,038 --> 00:03:41,824
by accessing the request body and then

79
00:03:42,019 --> 00:03:42,229
there,

80
00:03:43,429 --> 00:03:46,904
It will be the goal field that holds the

81
00:03:46,904 --> 00:03:49,848
entered text because this input has a name

82
00:03:49,944 --> 00:03:50,330
of goal

83
00:03:51,472 --> 00:03:54,138
and we can extract the submitted data by

84
00:03:54,418 --> 00:03:55,503
using that name.

85
00:03:57,380 --> 00:03:59,475
So since I chose name goal here,

86
00:04:00,173 --> 00:04:03,438
request body will have a goal property which

87
00:04:03,568 --> 00:04:04,867
holds the entered text.

88
00:04:06,515 --> 00:04:09,350
Now we could add some validation here to

89
00:04:09,350 --> 00:04:11,631
check whether some valid value has been

90
00:04:11,631 --> 00:04:14,600
entered, But we didn't do that before and

91
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:16,463
instead that is something we'll explore

92
00:04:16,463 --> 00:04:18,829
later in this course, therefore I will not

93
00:04:18,829 --> 00:04:19,299
do it here.

94
00:04:20,572 --> 00:04:22,957
Instead, I'll simply go to my courseGoals

95
00:04:23,005 --> 00:04:26,245
array and push this goal text into it.

96
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:31,128
So with that, this array is updated and

97
00:04:31,241 --> 00:04:32,729
we're outputting this array down there

98
00:04:33,425 --> 00:04:35,382
but at the moment we

99
00:04:36,077 --> 00:04:38,471
wouldn't see any changes.

100
00:04:39,066 --> 00:04:41,984
In that list. And actually at the moment, we

101
00:04:42,513 --> 00:04:43,379
would basically

102
00:04:43,908 --> 00:04:46,217
send a request that doesn't get back a

103
00:04:46,217 --> 00:04:49,231
response because I am not sending back any

104
00:04:49,263 --> 00:04:52,534
response here in my goals POST route. And

105
00:04:52,630 --> 00:04:54,202
that's of course something that should

106
00:04:54,218 --> 00:04:54,442
change.

107
00:04:55,741 --> 00:04:58,178
And indeed it is that response that we wanna

108
00:04:58,178 --> 00:05:01,209
send back that will allow us to then also

109
00:05:01,209 --> 00:05:03,902
make sure that we update the screen and that

110
00:05:03,934 --> 00:05:07,013
we reflect all goals including the new goal

111
00:05:07,530 --> 00:05:08,953
after the form was submitted.

112
00:05:10,330 --> 00:05:13,480
And we can essentially use 2 different

113
00:05:13,496 --> 00:05:15,392
approaches here and I'll show you both,

114
00:05:15,907 --> 00:05:17,996
though of course it's fine if you just used

115
00:05:17,996 --> 00:05:19,652
one of them for your solution.

116
00:05:20,970 --> 00:05:24,926
The first possible approach is to redirect

117
00:05:25,216 --> 00:05:25,409
to

118
00:05:26,116 --> 00:05:27,406
the root route here.

119
00:05:29,035 --> 00:05:29,556
So to

120
00:05:30,403 --> 00:05:31,348
this GET route

121
00:05:31,869 --> 00:05:32,341
in the end.

122
00:05:33,217 --> 00:05:37,139
If we do that, HTMX will follow that

123
00:05:37,332 --> 00:05:40,016
redirect and therefore it will receive this

124
00:05:40,145 --> 00:05:42,219
entire page as a response.

125
00:05:43,685 --> 00:05:46,213
And that's good because this page will

126
00:05:46,744 --> 00:05:49,481
then include all the goals, including the

127
00:05:49,481 --> 00:05:51,898
latest goal, so the goal that was just

128
00:05:52,038 --> 00:05:52,282
added.

129
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:57,608
Therefore, we can select this part of the

130
00:05:57,608 --> 00:06:00,417
response this unordered list here

131
00:06:00,966 --> 00:06:04,112
and we can replace the unordered list of

132
00:06:04,208 --> 00:06:06,758
goals that we have on the current page with

133
00:06:06,870 --> 00:06:09,816
that new unordered list that we get back

134
00:06:09,947 --> 00:06:10,914
from the response.

135
00:06:12,582 --> 00:06:14,305
So that's one possible approach and I'll

136
00:06:14,353 --> 00:06:15,561
show you how it would work.

137
00:06:16,108 --> 00:06:18,298
Here I have response redirect

138
00:06:18,926 --> 00:06:19,393
and then

139
00:06:20,053 --> 00:06:24,012
on the form, I now also wanna add hx-select

140
00:06:24,336 --> 00:06:27,238
to control which part of the response is

141
00:06:27,449 --> 00:06:30,256
swapped into the currently loaded page.

142
00:06:31,653 --> 00:06:33,259
And in my case, that should be this

143
00:06:33,339 --> 00:06:34,077
unordered list.

144
00:06:35,025 --> 00:06:38,654
Now, as you learned, hx-select wants a CSS

145
00:06:38,718 --> 00:06:41,191
selector here that selects the part of the

146
00:06:41,191 --> 00:06:43,455
response that should be swapped in. And we

147
00:06:43,455 --> 00:06:46,762
could use ul here to select this unordered

148
00:06:46,810 --> 00:06:47,244
list

149
00:06:47,934 --> 00:06:51,306
and that would work. Or to mix things up, we

150
00:06:51,306 --> 00:06:53,008
could also select it by ID.

151
00:06:54,736 --> 00:06:57,532
And the ID CSS selector here would be

152
00:06:57,580 --> 00:06:57,776
#goals.

153
00:07:00,300 --> 00:07:03,475
So with that, we would select the right part

154
00:07:03,556 --> 00:07:05,776
of the response, so the part we want.

155
00:07:06,657 --> 00:07:08,525
And I'll now split this across multiple

156
00:07:08,525 --> 00:07:10,183
lines to make it a bit easier to read.

157
00:07:11,407 --> 00:07:14,354
Of course, I also wanna control where this

158
00:07:14,499 --> 00:07:16,547
selected response content is

159
00:07:17,209 --> 00:07:20,180
rendered on the existing page. So which part

160
00:07:20,357 --> 00:07:23,154
of the existing page is swapped for this

161
00:07:23,203 --> 00:07:24,354
response content.

162
00:07:25,893 --> 00:07:27,984
And we control that with hx-target.

163
00:07:30,613 --> 00:07:32,825
And the target of course should be the same

164
00:07:32,954 --> 00:07:35,425
unordered list, but now we're not targeting

165
00:07:35,457 --> 00:07:37,540
the list in the response, but instead on the

166
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:38,735
currently rendered page.

167
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:44,431
So again, we can use #goals here or the ul

168
00:07:44,559 --> 00:07:47,862
selector or any other CSS selector that

169
00:07:47,862 --> 00:07:49,038
selects that list of goals.

170
00:07:52,357 --> 00:07:55,723
Well, and then I also wanna control how the

171
00:07:55,723 --> 00:07:58,561
list is swapped. And we can control that

172
00:07:58,609 --> 00:08:00,532
with hx-swap.

173
00:08:01,719 --> 00:08:04,828
Here, the default is innerHTML, which means

174
00:08:05,165 --> 00:08:07,986
the content of the targeted list would be

175
00:08:07,986 --> 00:08:09,958
replaced with the content selected

176
00:08:10,535 --> 00:08:11,032
in the

177
00:08:11,673 --> 00:08:12,266
response.

178
00:08:12,940 --> 00:08:15,136
And that's actually not what I want because

179
00:08:15,136 --> 00:08:17,043
I'm selecting the entire list in my

180
00:08:17,108 --> 00:08:20,009
response. And if I would then just use that

181
00:08:20,009 --> 00:08:22,257
to replace the content of the list on the

182
00:08:22,257 --> 00:08:24,673
currently active page, I would render the

183
00:08:24,673 --> 00:08:27,330
response list inside of the existing list.

184
00:08:27,411 --> 00:08:30,615
So I would have nested lists and that's not

185
00:08:30,615 --> 00:08:31,137
what I want.

186
00:08:32,250 --> 00:08:34,605
So therefore what we want here instead is

187
00:08:35,193 --> 00:08:35,668
outerHTML,

188
00:08:36,660 --> 00:08:38,871
which makes sure that we replace the

189
00:08:38,871 --> 00:08:41,391
existing list with the list from the

190
00:08:41,408 --> 00:08:42,026
response.

191
00:08:43,975 --> 00:08:45,778
And that should then be all.

192
00:08:46,309 --> 00:08:49,690
With these HTMX attributes added to the

193
00:08:49,690 --> 00:08:49,947
form,

194
00:08:50,625 --> 00:08:53,353
We should be able to save everything and we

195
00:08:53,353 --> 00:08:55,323
should be able to add goals here.

196
00:08:59,970 --> 00:09:00,789
And as you can tell,

197
00:09:01,930 --> 00:09:04,790
this seems to work here since these goals

198
00:09:04,967 --> 00:09:06,140
are showing up here.

199
00:09:07,490 --> 00:09:10,528
So that's one way of solving this and it's

200
00:09:10,528 --> 00:09:13,231
an absolutely fine way of solving this.

201
00:09:14,390 --> 00:09:16,385
But there also is an alternative.

202
00:09:17,659 --> 00:09:21,030
Instead of redirecting here, we could also

203
00:09:21,367 --> 00:09:23,165
directly return some

204
00:09:23,759 --> 00:09:28,270
HTML fragment that can then be used by HTMX.

205
00:09:28,832 --> 00:09:31,288
And therefore here, we could directly send

206
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:31,657
back

207
00:09:32,508 --> 00:09:36,987
the updated list or actually maybe just that

208
00:09:37,019 --> 00:09:40,551
one list item that was added because why

209
00:09:40,615 --> 00:09:43,585
would we send back the entire updated list?

210
00:09:43,907 --> 00:09:46,999
It's just one new list item that's added

211
00:09:46,999 --> 00:09:50,156
here. So why don't we just send back that,

212
00:09:50,723 --> 00:09:52,116
that one list item?

213
00:09:53,690 --> 00:09:55,258
So therefore that's what I'm doing here. I'm

214
00:09:55,258 --> 00:09:57,376
sending back a new list item

215
00:09:57,991 --> 00:09:58,217
which

216
00:09:58,961 --> 00:10:00,319
outputs the goal text

217
00:10:01,629 --> 00:10:04,898
and which should also have an ID to be in

218
00:10:04,898 --> 00:10:07,400
line with the other list items here, that is

219
00:10:07,662 --> 00:10:08,218
goal-index.

220
00:10:11,893 --> 00:10:15,257
So goal dash, and then the question is, what

221
00:10:15,257 --> 00:10:17,974
is the index of that list item? Well, since

222
00:10:18,087 --> 00:10:20,965
I'm pushing it into this array, it will be

223
00:10:21,335 --> 00:10:23,282
the last item in that array.

224
00:10:24,892 --> 00:10:28,706
So it's courseGoals.length minus 1,

225
00:10:30,590 --> 00:10:33,134
courseGoals.length minus 1.

226
00:10:34,035 --> 00:10:36,434
That will be the index of this newly added

227
00:10:36,788 --> 00:10:37,255
list item.

228
00:10:38,192 --> 00:10:40,227
And with that, I'm just sending back this

229
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:44,089
HTML fragment, which is something you often

230
00:10:44,121 --> 00:10:47,887
do when working with HTMX and you have full

231
00:10:47,887 --> 00:10:50,723
control over the backend because that then

232
00:10:50,931 --> 00:10:51,764
allows us to

233
00:10:52,437 --> 00:10:53,158
change that

234
00:10:53,719 --> 00:10:55,786
frontend code, this HTMX code.

235
00:10:57,260 --> 00:11:00,657
We no longer need to select anything from

236
00:11:00,705 --> 00:11:03,333
the response because now the entire response

237
00:11:03,413 --> 00:11:05,980
is just what we need. So we can get rid of

238
00:11:05,980 --> 00:11:06,237
that.

239
00:11:07,345 --> 00:11:10,670
And of course now we need to change hx-swap

240
00:11:11,376 --> 00:11:12,918
because I'm still targeting my

241
00:11:13,464 --> 00:11:16,371
list of goals, but now I don't wanna replace

242
00:11:16,580 --> 00:11:19,712
the entire list with that one list item I

243
00:11:19,728 --> 00:11:22,025
get back in my response. Instead, I wanna

244
00:11:22,057 --> 00:11:26,602
append that one list item after the existing

245
00:11:26,618 --> 00:11:27,759
items in that list.

246
00:11:28,963 --> 00:11:31,196
And we can do that with the before-after

247
00:11:32,409 --> 00:11:35,920
which will insert the response content into

248
00:11:36,212 --> 00:11:39,884
the targeted element after all the elements

249
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:43,473
that are already in the targeted element.

250
00:11:45,628 --> 00:11:46,537
And with that done,

251
00:11:47,299 --> 00:11:48,906
if we save that and reload,

252
00:11:49,652 --> 00:11:51,906
and I again start adding goals

253
00:11:55,741 --> 00:11:56,113
like this,

254
00:11:56,967 --> 00:11:57,481
you see

255
00:11:58,093 --> 00:12:00,505
that still works, though I of course forgot

256
00:12:00,505 --> 00:12:02,998
one thing, that remove button here, that

257
00:12:02,998 --> 00:12:03,770
should also be there.

258
00:12:04,962 --> 00:12:08,348
Therefore, I'll quickly go back and actually

259
00:12:08,429 --> 00:12:12,106
copy this structure inside such a goal list

260
00:12:12,219 --> 00:12:12,477
item

261
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:16,285
and replace my goal text here

262
00:12:16,898 --> 00:12:19,044
with that structure. And that should again

263
00:12:19,076 --> 00:12:21,900
be goal text so that we send back

264
00:12:22,499 --> 00:12:23,779
a list item

265
00:12:24,524 --> 00:12:24,994
like this.

266
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:30,655
But with that change in place,

267
00:12:31,318 --> 00:12:32,499
if I now reload,

268
00:12:34,522 --> 00:12:37,596
that looks much better here. And that's an

269
00:12:37,596 --> 00:12:39,777
alternative way of solving this.
